A||N||8||DisfourDan||Found a Fiero, Need advice||||1||
Z||000000||DisfourDan||05-25-2001||10:33 AM||||Description:  2.8L, FAST!!!Runs great, BRAND SPANKIN new tires, NEW BRAKES! all new exhaust gaskets, new windshield, oil change, current smog and all dmv reg paid up low miles, invested over $1300 in the past 2 weeks all receipts!   <BR>Features:  Automatic Transmission · Power Windows · Power Locks · One Owner · Air Conditioning   <P>57000 miles<BR>going for 2000$ or best offer.  I am going to go check it out soon, and I am taking my dad with me, so we can test drive it.<P>------------------<BR>Nothing good can come from good.||||reg||1
Z||000001||thomas_l||05-25-2001||10:43 AM||||Looks like a good deal. Of course year and model might define just how good a deal...||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ken Wittlief||05-25-2001||10:47 AM||||sounds great esp for $2k or BO<P> but be carefull and listen for defensive statements from the owner!<P> if he just spent $1500 on it, esp if he paid someone else to do the work<P> and now he is bailing out of the car<P> it could be something bad was discovered while all that work was being done<P>  ya gotta be cold hearted - objective - and clear headed when looking at a used car<P>  your hearts gonna be telling you: Its beautify, BUY IT! BUY IT! BUY IT!<P>  but you gotta be cold hearted and skeptical - if the seller gives you any indication of serious trouble with the car - walk away! Even if you let a good deal get away from you - there were over 200,000 Fieros producted - still plenty more out there for you.<P>   Get the VIN number off the dash and post it here (someone on this forum has CarFax (c:<P>  and if there is anything fishy about the car get on here and post what you see - you got 2000 fiero addicts here at your beck and call!<P>   If the car is really great and you have some reservations put the smallest deposit down you can to hold the car for a day or so while you think it though and get some feedback from us. Even if you put $100 down, and back out and loose it, you can do a lot worse on a used car that loosing $100.<P>  If its great see if he'll hold it for $50.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DisfourDan||05-25-2001||10:48 AM||||I guess it is only a Fiero, it does not state if it is SE,GT or any of the other models.  Its only about an hour away from me.  So ill go an check it out when she responds to my email.<P>------------------<BR>Nothing good can come from good.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ken Wittlief||05-25-2001||10:52 AM||||Things to look for:<P>New windshield?! Why? dont ask him - look at the car, was it wrecked? any rippled sheet metal under the front hood?<P>  brand new tires? Why? look at the front end. Take a hydralic floor jack and raise the wheels and pull and twist them. Any thing loose? clunking? New tires may have been required cause the front end is badly out of alignment - or again, maybe the car was wrecked?<P>  look for new paint on the front hood or bumer too. If he only hit a deer its not a bad thing (unless you are in the car at the time)<P>  if the whole front clip has been replaced... :-O||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrgone||05-25-2001||05:48 PM||||look for rubber spray under the rear, he may have said "lets roast these babies off before i sell it"<P>hehe||||reg||1
Z||000006||sqoach||05-25-2001||05:58 PM||||Sounds like a good deal. But be careful. You said he just put lots of money into it. Probably just so it can sell. Or maybe he was considering keeping it. Do you know why he's selling so cheap? Is it a stock color? Everyone else has already given some good things to look for. Tell us what you find out.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach2.JPG">   <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||1
Z||000007||DisfourDan||05-25-2001||06:34 PM||||the guy said it was donated to them.  I do not think I will even bother, seeing as to it is an automatic, and it is not the year i want.  I have waited two years for this car, i think i can wait a bit longer.<P>------------------<BR>Nothing good can come from good.||||reg||7
Z||000008||sjp777||05-25-2001||08:25 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DisfourDan:<BR><B>the guy said it was donated to them.  I do not think I will even bother, seeing as to it is an automatic, and it is not the year i want.  I have waited two years for this car, i think i can wait a bit longer.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Good idea, hold out for a 4 or 5 speed. I looked for 3 years before I bought my GT. If you buy one that is really not what you want you will suffer from intense Fiero envy and you'll never fully bond with your car. These cars can put you through hell, and if you don't really love it, you'll grow to hate it.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_2.jpg">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||14
